  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2014-tumor-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2014-tumor-02--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2014-tumor-02--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2014-tumor-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.64" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Each listed hallmark has a standard assay and published measurements are available. Existing data can test the Xenopus phenotype but only partially address the comparison with the heterogeneous scope of human tumors." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Quantify proliferation, nuclear area, hypoxia, intracellular pH, and leukocyte recruitment in oncogene-induced structures versus matched unaffected tissue, then compare effect directions with standard tumor hallmarks. Consistent significant differences support phenotypic similarity." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Raw images and per-embryo measurements are not clearly deposited.", "Sharing hallmarks does not establish equivalence to human tumors." ;
